{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויברך אלהים", :translit "va-yevarekh elohim", :gloss "And Elohim blessed"} {:he "ויברך אלהים את נח", :translit "va-yevarekh elohim et noach", :gloss "And Elohim blessed Noah"} {:he "ויברך אלהים את יצחק", :translit "va-yevarekh elohim et yitzchak", :gloss "And Elohim blessed Isaac"} {:he "ג' דסמיכי", :translit "gimel de-samikhei", :gloss "three of juxtaposed (construct forms)"} {:he "עד עתה הייתי זקוק לברך את בריותי מכאן ואילך הברכות יהיו מסורים בידך", :translit "ad ata hayiti zaruikh levarekh et beriyotai mikan va-eilakh ha-berakhot yihyu mesurot be-yadekha", :gloss "Until now I needed to bless My creations; from here onward the blessings shall be placed in your hand"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["ויברך אלהים" "ויברך אלהים את נח" "ויברך אלהים את יצחק"]}], :frame {:text "The Midrash records that after the Akedah, God says to Isaac: 'Until now I needed to bless My creations; from here onward the blessings are placed in your hand' — found in Bereishit Rabbah 56:7 on Genesis 22:18. The idea that the Flood wiped out all prior beings and required a renewed blessing of the world appears in Bereishit Rabbah 11:6 on Genesis 2:3. The specific three-fold Masoretic list of juxtaposed 'ויברך אלהים' forms reflects the Masoretic annotation tradition of counting rare syntactic constructions.", :sources ["Bereishit Rabbah 56:7" "Bereishit Rabbah 11:6" "Genesis 2:3" "Genesis 22:18"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["ויברך אלהים" "ויברך אלהים את נח" "ויברך אלהים את יצחק"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ויברך אלהים", :refs ["Genesis 2:3" "Genesis 9:1" "Genesis 25:11"], :n 3, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ויברך אלהים את נח", :refs ["Genesis 9:1"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ויברך אלהים את יצחק", :refs ["Genesis 25:11"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:03:57.557769596Z", :m